meaning_in_context asked "which meaning best fits X?" but, for half of builds
(paraphrase_context rows), offered vocabulary headwords including the target.
Guards only covered typed activities, so choice activities were exempt.

- New semantic contract (src/vocabulary/meaning-context-contract.js) enforced in the
  builder (fail closed, logged), the content validator and tests.
- Shared marker: meaning_in_context accepts ONLY the meaning phrase designated for the
  context row (sense.masteryContexts). Headword, synonyms and every legacy accepted
  answer are wrong; no designation means nothing is correct. Other question types
  that share the same rows are unchanged. Requires the Edge Function to be redeployed.
- Unit 1: two curated inferential mastery contexts per target with definition-style
  options, anchored on the meaning/paraphrase rows (additive accepted_answers),
  plus a second, stricter human pass (22 variants reworded).
- Tests, audit fixture and docs/vocabulary-meaning-in-context-audit.md.

