+// Meaning → Mastery (meaning_in_context) content for Unit 1.
+//
+// Every target has TWO variants (A is anchored on the occurrence's `_meaning` context row, B on its `_paraphrase` row). Two
+// variants are required because Mastery needs at least two distinct prompts (promptKeys are derived from the context id), and
+// each variant gets its own correct meaning phrase so the learner cannot pass the second one by recognising an option string.
+//
+// Each variant gives the student the target word inside a realistic sentence whose surrounding evidence (a consequence, a
+// contrast, a purpose) lets them infer the meaning, and four MEANING options: one correct definition-style phrase and
+// three plausible but wrong ones in the same grammatical shape. The sentence never contains a known synonym or a copy
+// of the definition (see src/vocabulary/meaning-context-contract.js, enforced by the builder, the validator and the tests).
+//
+//   sentence   the context shown to the student (contains `focus`)
+//   focus      the exact surface form of the target in the sentence
+//   meaning    the correct answer: a definition-style phrase
+//   distractors three wrong meanings: opposite / neighbouring / plausible misunderstanding
+//   clue       (audit note only, not published) the evidence that lets a learner infer the meaning
